Phantom-WG on AWS EC2

    Stack                  {{ stack_name }}, in {{ region }}
    Phantom-WG Modern      {{ modern_address }}
    Phantom-Frontmatter    {{ front_address }}

    The commands of this guide run in the directory of the playbook:
    {{ playbook_dir }}
    The guide is kept there, in {{ setup_dir }}/guide.txt.

Dashboard

    https://{{ modern_address }}

    The certificate is self-signed. The username is admin. This command reads
    the password from the node:

    ssh -i {{ setup_dir }}/id_ed25519 admin@{{ modern_address }} cat /home/admin/phantom-wg/container-data/secrets/production/.admin_password

Clients

    A client is added in the dashboard, and its configuration is exported
    there. The configuration reaches Phantom-WG Modern directly, at
    {{ modern_address }}:51820 over UDP.

    To carry the client through Phantom-Frontmatter, add this block to the
    same configuration:

    {{ client_block | trim | indent(4) }}

Shell

    Phantom-WG Modern is in /home/admin/phantom-wg on its node, and
    ./tools/prod.sh help lists its commands:

    ssh -i {{ setup_dir }}/id_ed25519 admin@{{ modern_address }}

    On the node of Phantom-Frontmatter, sudo frontmatter-api ghost status
    reports the data path:

    ssh -i {{ setup_dir }}/id_ed25519 admin@{{ front_address }}

From here on the setup is yours

    Both security groups take their ports from every address, SSH among them.
    The rules are yours to narrow.
    The SSH key was made for this setup. Your own key goes on the nodes when
    you choose.
    Updates run on the nodes, with the commands of the two products.
    AWS bills the nodes and their addresses for as long as the stack stands.
    The playbook deletes nothing, and a second run leaves the stack as it is.
    To remove the setup, delete the stack {{ stack_name }} in CloudFormation, then
    the directory {{ setup_dir }}.
